    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "**And a source path moves under you. The worked example below was\n`docs/folio-assistant/proposals/bootstrap.md`; the stub pattern inverted it to\n`folio-assistant/docs/proposals/` (bean `wggr`), and then proposals were\nrelocated out of the site entirely to `fsh-guts/proposals/` — and back INTO it on\n2026-09-23, to `cat-harness/docs/proposals/`, on the owner's ruling that a\nproposal belongs in the `docs/` of the stub that needs it. The sentence is kept\nrather than rewritten because what it describes did happen; what is kept and\naddressable but **deliberately unpublished** — so that page has no URL at all\nnow. Three moves in one day, and a URL composed from any remembered source\npath would have been wrong after each. The third move is the worst case for\ncomposing, because the composed URL is not merely the wrong path: it asserts a\npage exists where the repository has decided none should.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean wggr",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "This is the same defect `AGENTS.md` records for generated README links —\n*\"It composed links instead of resolving them\"*, where all twenty-three\nchapter PDF links were 404 and always had been — arriving one layer up, in an\nagent's own reasoning rather than in a generator."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Present on the ref is not the same as SERVED — read the Pages deployment",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-09-20, on a repository with four concurrent agent sessions:\n**64 commits to `gh-pages` in 90 minutes**, and **6 of the last 10 Pages\ndeployments `cancelled`**. The pattern was exact rather than random — each\nstaging deploy pushes *two* commits about ten seconds apart, the payload\n(`staging(<slug>): from <sha>`) and then `render-log: rendered …`, and the second\nreliably cancels the first's build. Two pushes, two builds, one of them always\nwasted.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A clean check set and a COMPLETE check set are different questions",
      "prov:value": "The same hole one layer down cost real pushes. Measured twice on 2026-09-30:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A clean check set and a COMPLETE check set are different questions",
      "prov:value": "`check:head-has-run` (bean `3pqn`) already answers it — `coverageFor`\nreconciles the runs against the workflows the tree itself declares, and\n`mergeStateForHead` returns `conflicted` for the case below. `bun run cat ci:watch`\ncomposes both since #1664.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3pqn",
        "#1664"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A clean check set and a COMPLETE check set are different questions",
      "prov:value": "| cause | how it reads | what to do |\n|---|---|---|\n| **a conflicted head** | no `pull_request` run is published AT ALL — the forge mints no `refs/pull/N/merge`, and a `pull_request` run checks that ref out (bean `52cz`) | merge the base in. The checks are not slow; they are never coming |\n| **a filtered trigger that owed no run** | genuinely nothing was due | stay silent — `g62s` measured that loosening this produces false fires |\n| **a run never created, unexplained** | a workflow the tree declares `on: pull_request` has no run and the head is mergeable | a **finding** (bean `3pqn`), not a wait |\n| **a bot-actor push** | the runs EXIST and are `completed`, with `conclusion: action_required` — approval was owed and never given, so no job ran (bean `0qjq`) | read the dispatched run instead; see below |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 52cz",
        "bean 3pqn",
        "bean 0qjq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`conclusion: action_required` is not a failure, and not a pass",
      "prov:value": "Established by intervention rather than inference, on #1939, 2026-10-03 — four\nconsecutive commits alternating strictly with the pushing actor:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1939",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`conclusion: action_required` is not a failure, and not a pass",
      "prov:value": "`check:head-has-run` already reads it this way —\nits own header records crediting `Code-quality gates` via `workflow_dispatch`\nalone on #1222 — so do not add an event filter to it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1222"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`conclusion: action_required` is not a failure, and not a pass",
      "prov:value": "The consequence worth carrying: `MERGE_MAIN_TOKEN` (#1829 D1) is a\n**convenience**, not a correctness fix. It makes the PR's own runs fire on the\nbot's push instead of needing a dispatch. Saying the bot leaves its merges\nunproved is wrong, and a steward who believes it will hand-push commits to\n\"restore\" gates that already ran.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1829"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`conclusion: action_required` is not a failure, and not a pass",
      "prov:value": "A\n`pull_request` run tests the head merged with `main` as it was at push time, so\nmain moving flips verdicts in both directions with no change to your branch. On\n2026-09-30 it turned a green branch head into a red merge commit, and six\nminutes later turned a red check green when a sibling's fix landed mid-cycle. The second was diagnosed as a flapping gate; it was not. One command settles it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/github-state-inspection.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Order of resort",
      "prov:value": "## Where the agent goes wrong, measured"
    }
  ]
}
